# Validation

Platform-neutral gate:

```text
uv run --locked --managed-python python -B scripts/validate_ci.py
```

Rules:

- During iteration run only targeted checks for changed behavior and direct
  consumers. Do not run validation for read-only work.
- There is one full-gate owner per exact candidate fingerprint: Cursor, Codex,
  or GitHub CI. Never run the full gate merely because the same bytes moved
  from worktree to stage, commit, push, or PR.
- If Codex or CI is guaranteed to validate the same pushed head, return
  targeted evidence, the commit/tree identity, and
  `FULL_VALIDATION=DELEGATED_TO_CI`; this is a valid handoff, not a blocker.
- Run the full gate locally only when Cursor is the elected full-gate owner or
  downstream validation is unavailable.
- Re-run a failed check only after its root cause changed. Re-run a passed full
  gate only after candidate fingerprint, dependencies, relevant runtime, or
  validation policy changed.
- Apply Catalog/generator, security, topology, and cross-platform checks only
  when their owners or direct consumers changed.
- Do not weaken or patch validators merely to pass.
- Catalog and generated-consumer repair inside the active objective is covered
  by standing project autonomy; report unrelated Catalog drift honestly.
- Technical validation is not semantic acceptance or `DONE`.
- See `AGENTS.md` section `VALIDATION_COMMAND`.
